hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"73","Allāhumma innī as'aluka `ilman nāfi`an, wa rizqan ṭayyiban, wa `amalam-mutaqabbala. [to be said after giving salam for the Fajr prayer.] \O Allah"","" I ask You for knowledge which is beneficial"","" and sustenance which is good"","" and deeds which are acceptable.\"" Reference: Ibn Majah and others. See Sahih Ibn Majah 1/152 and Majma' Az-Zawa'id 10/111"""""
"74","Qāla Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāhi raḍiyallāhu ʿanhumā: Kāna Rasūlullāhi ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam, yuʿallimunā al-istikhāra fī al-umūri kullihā kamā yuʿallimunā al-sūrata min al-Qurʾān, yaqūlu: \Idhā hamma aḥadukum bi-al-amli fal-yarkaʿ rakʿatayni min ghayri al-farīḍati"","" thumma yaqul: 'Allāhumma innī astakhīruka bi-ʿilmika"","" wa astaqdiruka bi-qudratika"","" wa asʾaluka min faḍlika al-ʿaẓīm"","" fa-innaka taqdiru wa lā aqdiru"","" wa taʿlamu wa lā aʿlamu"","" wa Anta ʿAllām al-Ghuyūb. Allāhumma in kunta taʿlamu hādhā al-amra — yusammī ḥājatahu — khayran lī fī dīnī wa maʿāshī wa ʿāqibati amrī — aw qāla: ʿājilhi wa ājilhi — faqdurhu lī wa yassirhu lī"","" thumma bārik lī fīhi. Wa in kunta taʿlamu hādhā al-amra sharrun lī fī dīnī wa maʿāshī wa ʿāqibati amrī — aw qāla: ʿājilhi wa ājilhi — faṣrifhu ʿannī wa ṣrifnī ʿanhu"","" waqdur lī al-khayra ḥaythu kāna"","" thumma arḍinī bihi.' Wa mā nadima man istakhāra al-Khāliq"","" wa shāwara al-makhlūqīna al-muʾminīna wa thabbata fī amrihi"","" fa-qad qāla subḥānahu: 'Wa shāwirhum fī al-amr"","" fa-idhā ʿazamta fa-tawakkal ʿalā Allāh.'\"". Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh (may Allāh be pleased with both of them) said: The Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) used to teach us to seek guidance (istikhārah) in all matters"","" just as he would teach us a sūrah from the Qurʾān. He would say: \""When one of you intends to do something"","" let him pray two rakʿahs of voluntary prayer"","" then say: 'O Allāh"","" I seek Your guidance through Your knowledge"","" and I seek Your help through Your power"","" and I ask You from Your immense bounty. For You have power and I do not; You know and I do not know; and You are the Knower of the unseen. O Allāh"","" if You know that this matter — mentioning his need — is good for me in my religion"","" my livelihood"","" and the outcome of my affairs — or he said: its immediate and its eventual consequences — then decree it for me"","" make it easy for me"","" and bless me in it. And if You know that this matter is harmful for me in my religion"","" my livelihood"","" and the outcome of my affairs — or he said: its immediate and its eventual consequences — then turn it away from me and turn me away from it"","" and decree for me the good wherever it may be"","" then make me content with it.' And no one ever regretted seeking guidance from the Creator"","" consulting the believing creation"","" and being firm in his decision. For He"","" the Most High"","" said: 'And consult them in the matter. And when you have decided"","" then rely upon Allāh.'\"""""""
